Firmware built by the agent tools
---------------------------------

`jumper build` / the MCP `build` tool (services/runner) compile the user's own
sketch with the same pinned toolchain plus the libraries the project declares
in firmware.libraries. Those firmware images belong to the user and carry the
licenses of what they link: the Arduino AVR core (LGPL-2.1), avr-libc
(BSD-3-Clause) and each declared library. Besides the libraries above, the
runner image (services/runner/docker/Dockerfile) preinstalls:

  Servo 1.3.0                      GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1,
                                   Copyright (c) Michael Margolis, Arduino

Libraries that are not preinstalled are downloaded from the Arduino Library
Manager on first use, under their own licenses (some, e.g. NewPing, are GPL).

The full license texts ship with each package in node_modules.

RP2040 boards (round 5)
-----------------------

The RP2040 simulator backend (packages/sim-backends/src/rp2040) uses:

  rp2040js 1.4.1                   MIT License, Copyright (c) Uri Shaked
                                   (an open-source emulator library; no Wokwi
                                   parts or assets are used)

It does not include Raspberry Pi's RP2040 boot ROM. packages/sim-backends/src/
rp2040/rom.ts is an original implementation by the Jumper Authors of the ROM's
public function tables (as documented in the RP2040 datasheet and the pico-sdk
headers), so no ROM code is distributed.

RP2040 firmware (packages/sim-backends/fixtures/xiao_*.hex, pico_*.hex, and
anything `build` compiles for an RP2040 board) is built with the pinned image
toolchains/arduino-pico/Dockerfile and statically linked with:

  arduino-pico core 6.3.1          GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1,
  (rp2040:rp2040)                  Copyright (c) Earle F. Philhower, III and
                                   contributors
  Raspberry Pi pico-sdk (bundled   BSD-3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2020 Raspberry Pi
  in the core)                     (Trading) Ltd.
  TinyUSB (bundled in the core)    MIT License, Copyright (c) Ha Thach
                                   (tinyusb.org)
  newlib / libgcc (toolchain)      BSD-style / GPL with the GCC Runtime Library
                                   Exception

plus the Arduino libraries the sketch includes (the same pinned versions as
above). The arduino-pico sources are available from
https://github.com/earlephilhower/arduino-pico (tag 6.3.1); each fixture's
sketch sits next to its .hex and packages/sim-backends/fixtures/BUILD.md says
how to rebuild it.

Cases and the factory pack (packages/enclosure, round 6) use:

  replicad 1.1.0                   MIT License, Copyright (c) Steve Genoud
  replicad-opencascadejs 1.1.0     GNU Lesser General Public License 2.1
  (a WebAssembly build of          (Open CASCADE Technology, Copyright (c)
